## Bootstrap an admin user

The generated project includes an explicit, opt-in admin seed for the email-password provider. It never uses a built-in password and it keeps an existing user’s password unchanged.

Set the values only in your shell or deployment secret manager, then run:

```bash
export ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@example.com
export ADMIN_PASSWORD='replace-with-a-random-password'
export ADMIN_NAME='Administrator'
pnpm db:seed
```

The command is idempotent. It creates the user when absent, promotes the matching user to `admin`, and marks that user’s email as verified. It fails if the email-password provider is not enabled. To run it automatically after migrations during a controlled first deployment, set `SEED_ADMIN_ON_STARTUP=true` together with the three `ADMIN_*` variables. Keep `SEED_ADMIN_ON_STARTUP=false` for normal restarts and never commit these values.

